From 989f98fe3e92a5874e488c26b7b452cceee09150 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gryphon397 <jgfillman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 22:39:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] stoat: voice-state ready handling, online propagation,
 availability status

Fork-local changes to the API client, carried on top of 44d45ade.

- EventClient: request the full 'ready' field set explicitly. Specifying
  any ready param switches the server into selective mode, so asking for
  voice_states alone silently dropped users/servers/channels/members/
  emojis from the ready payload.
- v1 handleEvent: apply voice_states after ready + a tick, inside batch(),
  and only for participants whose user is already hydrated. Applying them
  inline raced the UI's first render and produced voice tiles with no
  user data.
- Server.syncMembers: propagate the online flag when hydrating users from
  a member fetch. Upstream's hydrateIfNotHas() returns undefined for users
  already in the collection, so their presence is never refreshed; collect
  those and update them inside the existing batch() rather than in the
  hydration loop, which upstream deliberately keeps out of batch.
- User.statusMessage: render the Stoat '__avail__<epoch_ms>' status-text
  convention as 'Available in Xm/Xh' or 'Available at HH:MM'.

Not pushable -- origin is stoatchat/javascript-client-sdk, which we do
not own. Patch is vendored in the parent repo under patches/submodules/.
